  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Elite Express operates as a last-mile delivery provider with heavy reliance on its FedEx ISP agreement. The recent renewal boosted fixed service‑charge revenue as activity‑based work also grew, and gross margins expanded, signaling improving operating leverage. However, the stock is an illiquid micro‑cap, leaving it highly volatile on limited news. Core demand appears stable, but client concentration risk remains a key watchpoint.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership steered the company through a public‑listing transition that caused a sharp, mostly one‑time surge in professional fees, payroll, and franchise taxes. While the team secured better contract terms with FedEx and gross margins improved, heavy overhead drove a deep net loss, eroding credibility. An analyst upgrade to a still‑negative “sell” rating and the stock’s depressed price suggest the market questions whether management can translate operational gains into sustainable profitability.",
